.TH AIO-TUI 1 "August 2026" "aio 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aio-tui \- aio text user interface (curses)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aio --tui
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launches the full-screen curses interface. A shared picker
.RB ( tui_pick )
backs every list: use arrow keys to move and Enter to launch the selected
game.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B l , b
Open the built-in pygame examples list.
.TP
.B p
Open the PyPI packages list.
.TP
.B g
Open the GitHub repos list.
.TP
.B a
Open the awesome-pygame list.
.TP
.B i
Prompt for a package name and launch it from PyPI.
.TP
.B v
Open the pygame version manager (install a specific pygame version).
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.PP
Within a list, arrows move, Enter launches, Esc or q returns to the main
menu.
.SH LAUNCHING
Selecting an entry launches it exactly as the CLI would: built-in examples
via
.BR "python -m pygame.examples.<name>" ,
PyPI packages via
.BR "python -m <pkg>" ,
and GitHub/awesome repositories by cloning and locating an entry point.
Missing modules are auto-installed and the launch retried once.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aio (1),
.BR aio-cli (1),
.BR aio-suite (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Jimmy + opencode
